e of them  becomes Samaritan a righteous superhero  who uses his powers to fight for justice  while his twin Nemesis uses them for  Revenge to get back at those who have  wronged them in this way Nemesis becomes  a symbol for the downtrodden a symbol to  stand up against of Oppression even if  it means through violence Granite City  becomes the perfect backdrop for this  because of the city's unrest working  class folk either can't find work or are  terribly underpaid Sam's mother can  barely make ends meet with her job as a  nurse and even gets evicted for a brief  time when she can't pay the bills an  event which forces Sam to seek out  dangerous jobs including stealing copper  wire and getting involved with a local  gang leader named Cyrus Cyrus is a huge  believer in nemesis's cause for Cyrus  Samaritan was a superhero who propped up  the status quo and defended the rich  Elites to him Samaritan was just another  cop  protect the rich one the rest of us went  hungry but Nemesis was the guy fighting  for the common folk a guy ready to start  a revolution for the downtrodden to rise  up his obsession with Nemesis is what  Spurs him to break into the police  department's evidence locker and reclaim  his legendary Hammer a hammer forged  with all of nemesis's hate and  apparently the only weapon that can  damage him and his brother but what  happened to Samaritan and Nemesis where  are they in present-day Granite City if  you believe the official reports the two  battled it out at a power plant where a  giant explosion took both their lives  but as we'll find out that's not exactly  how it went down Sam is obsessed with  Samaritan believing along with local  Bookshop and Samaritan conspiracy  theorist Albert casler that Samaritan  still lives when Sam is saved by Joe  from a group of local Thugs and  Witnesses his strength and ability to  crush a knife with his bare hands he  knows that Joe is Samaritan the two form  an unlikely friendship and I'd like to  think that Joe who grew up without a  father sees a bit of himself in Sam who  also doesn't have a father he'll later  tell Sam how lucky he is for having a  mom that cares for him Joe lost both of  his parents even Joe's hobby fixing  broken things is a metaphor for his life  he believes people like the objects he  repairs deserve a second chance no  friction that helps me relax and focus  and I figure some of these old things  deserve a second chance Sam watches Joe  miraculously heal after being run over  by a car solidifying that Joe is  Samaritan but we also see how Joe's  Powers come with their own limitations  every time he takes a huge beating  whether it be from a car or gang members  pummeling him with lead his body  overheats if he doesn't cool down  quickly his heart will literally explode  this is why he has a fridge jam-packed  with ice cream it helps him cool down so  when Cyrus finds out that Samaritan is  still alive after Joe saves the life of  a young girl and is caught on camera  Cyrus uses Sam as bait to lure Samaritan  to the local power plant to finish what  Nemesis started I also think it's no  coincidence that Cyrus wants to quote  bring power back to the People by  literally turning off the power he's  acquired these blackout bombs which shut  down any and all Electronics which  you'll use in an attempt to get the city  to rise up against its oppressive ruling  class so Joe who was moments away from  leaving town after his identity was  discovered has a change of heart coming  back to save the kid he's developed an  unlikely friendship with he uses his  garbage truck to Ram into Cyrus's base  and makes quick work of most of his men  their bullets doing absolutely no damage  to his body but Cyrus has Samaritan's  only weakness nemesis's Hammer he's able  to get the upper hand on Joe but not  before we're hit with the film's big  twist Joe isn't Samaritan he's actually  Nemesis years ago when Samaritan and  Nemesis battled it out at the power  plant S